    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "`AxNat.modEq d a b` is defined as `exists u v, a + d*u = b + d*v` -- the difference-free form, since natural subtraction is truncated. This is the compatibility property that makes modular arithmetic a ring quotient rather than a notation. formal.statement is the type the kernel admitted, taken verbatim from Kernel::render_lean over the environment build_nat_prelude produces; it was not transcribed by hand. The sort renders as `AxNat` (the prelude's own inductive) while declarations are rooted at `Nat`.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "d637d83f77dbfa43c98eee4ab0ad78d235099006",
